---
import Slide from '@decks/templates/Slide.astro';

// The component's documentation, running rather than pictured, rising
// off the bottom edge of the slide.
//
// The bleed is the same move `5-MCWhatIsMissionCloud` and `6-MCBeta`
// make with an image, and it is doing the same job here: a page that
// runs off the bottom reads as a page, where one boxed inside the slide
// reads as a screenshot of a page. Rounded top corners and square
// bottom, because the bottom is not an edge, it is a cut.
//
// `BleedImage` cannot do this. Its `bleed` prop only sets an edge to
// offset 0; extending past one needs a negative offset written inline,
// which is why this is positioned by hand. Same reason the two image
// slides above are raw `<img>` rather than the template.
//
// The page fills the frame with no gutters, which is deliberate and is
// what the width is chosen for. A centred fixed-width shell leaves a
// margin down each side, and that margin reads as "this is the whole
// site, and it has one component in it". Filling the frame reads as the
// inner page of a larger system whose component list is cropped off the
// left edge, which is the truthful impression: this is one page of a
// design system, not a design system.
//
// The contents nav sits on the right for the same reason. On the left it
// would read as the site's primary navigation and put us back where we
// started.
//
// What to say over it. The address under the specimen is the part that
// is not in every design system's docs: pick a state and the specimen
// and the address change together. Named values only, unknown values
// ignored rather than guessed at, so an agent can open a state and look
// at it instead of reading a paragraph describing one.
//
// Say the caveat before the engineer does. The vocabulary grew on the
// prototypes and documents the states the component has; it is not
// generated from the component. The claim is that the property should
// carry into the docs, not that these are generated docs today.
//
// Drive it, roughly in this order:
//   pick two or three states and let the address change under them
//   hover a row, open the row menu, take Move up
//   scroll to Props or States if anybody asks what else is in it, and to
//     Open questions if they ask what is not finished
---

<Slide subtitle="Docs">
	<iframe
		src="/decks/2026-checklist-component/docs?compact=1&scale=1&state=default"
		title="The Checklist component documentation, live"
		class="live-embed absolute left-1/2 m-0! block h-[930px] w-[1400px] max-h-none! max-w-none! -translate-x-1/2 rounded-t-2xl! border-0"
		style="bottom: -60px;"
	></iframe>
</Slide>
